Index,SS / Module,Feature,Test Case Name,Test Description,Meta Test Description,Speed,Mode,Memory Start Offset,Memory End Offset,Remarks,Test Steps / Procedure,Meta Test Steps / Procedure,Impacted Registers,Meta Impacted Registers,Validation / Acceptance Criteria,Meta Validation / Acceptance Criteria,Code Generation (Required / Not),Meta Headers,Meta Macros,Meta Arrays
"1","GPIO","GPIO Register Reset Defaults and Masked Read/Write Validation","gpio_reg_wr_rd_test","Validate that GPIO GP0 per-pin configuration registers 8–27 power up to their documented defaults and that masked write/read-back operations preserve non-writable fields and obey read/write masks.","The test runs two phases on a fixed list of 20 GPIO GP0 per-pin registers (8..27). Phase 1 (reset check): For each entry i, if skip_rst_array[i] == 1 or read_mask_array[i] == 0, the address is skipped. Otherwise, it reads the register and masks out bit[0] with 0xFFFFFFFE, then compares the result to default_value_array[i]. Any mismatch increments def_fail_cnt and prints an error. Phase 2 (masked write/read): It iterates six data patterns {0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000}. For each pattern, it writes (data_wr & write_mask_array[i]) to each address if skip_array[i] == 0 and write_mask_array[i] != 0. Then it reads back (read_reg(addr) & read_mask_array[i]) and computes exp_val = (data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | ((~write_mask_array[i]) & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i]). If data_rd != exp_val, wr_fail_cnt is incremented and an error is printed. At the end, if either def_fail_cnt > 0 or wr_fail_cnt > 0, finish(1) else finish(0). A soft reset helper is present but compiled out (#ifdef 0).","NA","NA","0x00000000","0x00000000","Reset-value checks ignore bit[0] to avoid false mismatches caused by input behavior. Registers with zero read/write masks are skipped appropriately. Arrays enumerate exactly 20 per-pin configuration registers (8–27). Note: CNT is set to 49 while the arrays contain 20 elements; ensure loop bounds align with array sizes to prevent out-of-bounds access during execution.","1) For each GP0_GPIO_8 to GP0_GPIO_27 register, verify the reset value equals the documented default while ignoring bit[0]. 2) For each of six predefined data patterns, write masked values to each writable register and then read back with the read mask applied. 3) For each register, confirm the read-back value matches the expected value that preserves non-writable fields at their default values. 4) Record any mismatches; the test passes if no default-value or write/read mismatches are detected.","1) Initialization: def_fail_cnt = 0; wr_fail_cnt = 0. 2) Reset/default verification (chk_rst_val): for i in [0..CNT-1]: addr = addr_array[i]; if (skip_rst_array[i] == 1) continue; if (read_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000) continue; data_rd = read_reg(addr); data = (data_rd & 0xFFFFFFFE); if (data != default_value_array[i]) { def_fail_cnt++; printf failure log }. 3) Masked write/read (chk_rd_wr): define chk_val[6] = {0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000}. For each pattern j: data_wr = chk_val[j]; 3a) Write loop: for i in [0..CNT-1]: addr = addr_array[i]; if (skip_array[i] == 1) continue; if (write_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000) continue; write_reg(addr, (data_wr & write_mask_array[i])); 3b) Read/compare loop: for i in [0..CNT-1]: addr = addr_array[i]; if (skip_array[i] == 1) continue; if (write_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000) continue; if (read_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000) continue; data_rd = (read_reg(addr) & read_mask_array[i]); wr_n = (write_mask_array[i] ^ 0xFFFFFFFF); exp_val = ((data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | (wr_n & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i])); if (data_rd != exp_val) { wr_fail_cnt++; printf mismatch log }. 4) Completion: if (def_fail_cnt > 0 || wr_fail_cnt > 0) finish(1) else finish(0).","gp0_gpio_8; GP0_GPIO_9; GP0_GPIO_10; GP0_GPIO_11; GP0_GPIO_12; GP0_GPIO_13; GP0_GPIO_14; GP0_GPIO_15; GP0_GPIO_16; GP0_GPIO_17; GP0_GPIO_18; GP0_GPIO_19; GP0_GPIO_20; GP0_GPIO_21; GP0_GPIO_22; GP0_GPIO_23; GP0_GPIO_24; GP0_GPIO_25; GP0_GPIO_26; GP0_GPIO_27","MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8..MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_DEFAULT_VAL..GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27_DEFAULT_VAL; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_READ_MASK..GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27_READ_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_WRITE_MASK..GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27_WRITE_MASK","PASS if for all non-skipped, readable GP0_GPIO_8–GP0_GPIO_27 registers, the reset value (ignoring bit[0]) matches the documented default, and for each data pattern, the read-back equals the expected value derived from the read/write masks and defaults with no mismatches.","Reset check: (read_reg(addr) & 0xFFFFFFFE) == default_value_array[i] for all i where skip_rst_array[i] == 0 and read_mask_array[i] != 0. Write/read check: data_rd = (read_reg(addr) & read_mask_array[i]); exp_val = ((data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | ((~write_mask_array[i]) & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i])); require data_rd == exp_val for all i and all j in chk_val where skip_array[i] == 0 and write_mask_array[i] != 0 and read_mask_array[i] != 0. Final PASS condition: def_fail_cnt == 0 and wr_fail_cnt == 0 at finish().","NA","#include <stdio.h>; #include <stdlib.h>; #include \"test_common.h\"; #include \"test_define.c\"; #include <gpio/gpio_def.h>; #include <gpio/gpio_offset.h>","#define CNT 49; #define SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS 0x00000000; #define SOFT_RST_REG_DATA 0x00000000","addr_array[20] = {MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8..MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27}; default_value_array[20] = {GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_DEFAULT_VAL..GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27_DEFAULT_VAL}; read_mask_array[20] = {GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_READ_MASK..GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27_READ_MASK}; write_mask_array[20] = {GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_WRITE_MASK..GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27_WRITE_MASK}; skip_array[20] = {0..0}; skip_rst_array[20] = {0..0}; chk_val[6] = {0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000}"
,"2","GPIO","interrupts can be generated based on negative edge detection at GPIO input","test_gpio_negedge_intr_en","Validate that each GPIO pad (8–39) generates a negative-edge interrupt when enabled and that per-pin and group interrupt status can be cleared correctly, including system-level status and GIC handling.","The test enables the appropriate GIC interrupt (87 for GPIO0 or 88 for GPIO1) and the corresponding system-level interrupt enable bit. It presets the external GPIO pad driver at 0xA0243FFC to 0xFFFFFFFF. For i = 0..31: programs per-pin control at base (MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + i*4) with bits [20,18,16] set, then for each pin computes wr_val=1<<i, clears raw status via MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_INTR_RAW_STCLR1, enables only that pin in MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, arms int_pend=1, toggles the external pad from 1 to ~wr_val to create a falling edge, and waits (timeout=5000 with wait_on(10)) for int_pend to be cleared by the ISR. On timeout, logs error and increments test_err. In Default_IRQHandler: sets int_pend=0, forces pads high (0xFFFFFFFF), reads per-pin register for the active i; if bit[0] (input state) is set, increments test_err; if bit[1] (edge status) is set, reads group status (MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1) and verifies the bit for the pin is set; clears per-pin latched status by writing bits [20,16] and clears raw status via MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_INTR_RAW_STCLR1; confirms group status is 0; clears system RAW_STCR1 GPIOx bit and clears the corresponding GIC IRQ; if bit[1] was not set, increments test_err. Test ends with finish(test_err).","NA","ISR","0xA0243FFC","0xA0243FFC","External pad drive at 0xA0243FFC is used to generate falling edges. Compile-time selection (GPIO0 or GPIO1) determines which GIC IRQ and system interrupt bits are used. An int_pend flag is used to synchronize test-case wait loops with ISR execution and enforce timeouts.","1) Enable the appropriate GIC interrupt and system-level GPIO interrupt output for the target block. 2) Configure all GPIO pins (8–39) for negative-edge detection and clear any stale raw status. 3) For each pin, enable only that pin’s interrupt, arm the ISR handshake, and drive a falling edge via the external pad control. 4) Wait for ISR completion with a timeout; flag any timeout as an error. 5) In the ISR, verify the per-pin edge status and the group status bit for the pin are asserted, then clear per-pin latched and raw status and confirm the group status clears. 6) Clear the system-level pending status and the GIC interrupt. 7) Pass if all pins complete without timeouts and all expected status/clear checks succeed.","test_case(): test_err=0; Conditionally GIC_EnableIRQ(87/88); Conditionally write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIOx_INTR); write_reg(0xA0243FFC, 0xFFFFFFFF); For i=0..31: addr1 = (MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + i*4); write_reg(addr1, (1u<<20)|(1u<<18)|(1u<<16)); wait_on(10); For i=0..31: wr_val = 1u<<i; write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_INTR_RAW_STCLR1, wr_val); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, wr_val); wait_on(10); int_pend=1; write_reg(0xA0243FFC, 0xFFFFFFFF); wait_on(30); write_reg(0xA0243FFC, ~wr_val); timeout=5000; while(int_pend && timeout--) wait_on(10); if(timeout==0){ printf timeout; test_err++; } finish(test_err). Default_IRQHandler(): local_wr=1u<<i; int_pend=0; write_reg(0xA0243FFC, 0xFFFFFFFF); raddr=(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + i*4); rdata=read_reg(raddr); if((rdata & 0x1)!=0) test_err++; if((rdata & 0x2)!=0){ rdata_grp=read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); if((rdata_grp & local_wr)==0) test_err++; raddr2=(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + i*4); write_reg(raddr2,(1u<<20)|(1u<<16)); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_INTR_RAW_STCLR1, local_wr); rdata_grp=read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); if(rdata_grp!=0) test_err++; Conditionally write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIOx_INTR); Conditionally GIC_ClearIRQ(87/88); } else { test_err++; }","gp0_gpio_8; GP0_GPIO_9; GP0_GPIO_10; GP0_GPIO_11; GP0_GPIO_12; GP0_GPIO_13; GP0_GPIO_14; GP0_GPIO_15; GP0_GPIO_16; GP0_GPIO_17; GP0_GPIO_18; GP0_GPIO_19; GP0_GPIO_20; GP0_GPIO_21; GP0_GPIO_22; GP0_GPIO_23; GP0_GPIO_24; GP0_GPIO_25; GP0_GPIO_26; GP0_GPIO_27","MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8..MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27 (+ i*4); MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1; MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_INTR_RAW_STCLR1; MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1; LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO0_INTR; LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO1_INTR; MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1; LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR; LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO1_INTR","PASS if each pin 8–39 produces a negative-edge interrupt when enabled, the ISR clears the per-pin latched and raw status, the group status returns to 0, the system-level pending status is cleared, and no timeouts occur.","Timeout loop: int_pend must become 0 before timeout reaches 0. On ISR entry, (rdata & 0x1) should be 0; (rdata & 0x2) should be nonzero; group status (read from MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1) must include (1<<i); after clearing per-pin (write (1<<20)|(1<<16)) and raw status, group status must be 0; after writing MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1 with the GPIOx bit, a subsequent read must indicate the bit is cleared; test_err must remain 0 at finish().","NA","#include <stdio.h>; #include <lss_sysreg.h>; #include \"test_define.c\"; #include <test_common.h>","#define CNT 49","addr_array[20] = {MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8..MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27}; default_value_array[20] = {GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_DEFAULT_VAL..GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27_DEFAULT_VAL}; read_mask_array[20] = {GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_READ_MASK..GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27_READ_MASK}; write_mask_array[20] = {GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_WRITE_MASK..GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27_WRITE_MASK}; skip_array[20] = {0..0}"
,"3","GPIO","interrupts can be generated based on positive edge detection at GPIO input","test_gpio_pedge_all_pads_en","Enable positive-edge interrupts for all GPIO pads (8–39), generate a rising edge per pad, and verify interrupt generation, servicing, and clearing at per-pin, group, and system levels without timeouts.","The test enables the appropriate GIC interrupt (87 for GPIO0 or 88 for GPIO1) and the corresponding system-level interrupt output. It programs per-pin control for i=0..31 at (MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + i*4) with 0x00020000 (enable posedge). It sets GPIOs 8–39 as inputs via MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1..4 = 0x000000FF. It enables all group interrupts via MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1 = 0xFFFFFFFF. For each i: drives pads low (0x00000000) at 0xA0243FFC, arms int_pend=1, then drives high (0xFFFFFFFF) to create a rising edge and waits (timeout=2000 with wait_on(10)) until int_pend==0; on timeout, logs error, increments test_err, and breaks. In Default_IRQHandler: reads group status (MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1) and masks the group enable; if nonzero, proceeds, else logs error. It clears per-pin raw status by writing 0x00010000 to each per-pin register across j=0..31, waits briefly, then verifies group status is 0. It clears system RAW_STCR1 GPIOx bit and verifies the bit is cleared on readback. It re-enables group interrupts and clears the GIC IRQ. The test ends with finish(test_err).","NA","ISR","0xA0243FFC","0xA0243FFC","Rising edges are generated using the external pad control at 0xA0243FFC. Compile-time selection (GPIO0 or GPIO1) determines the GIC IRQ and system status bits. The ISR masks group enable during service to avoid nested events, then re-enables after clearing.","1) Enable the appropriate GIC interrupt and system-level GPIO interrupt output. 2) Configure all per-pin control registers for positive-edge detection and set GPIOs 8–39 as inputs. 3) Enable the group interrupt output for all pads. 4) For each pad, drive a rising edge using the external control, waiting for ISR completion with timeout protection; flag timeouts. 5) In the ISR, confirm group status is asserted, clear per-pin raw status across all pins, verify group status clears, and clear system-level status. 6) Re-enable group interrupt output and repeat for remaining pins. 7) Pass if all pads trigger and clear correctly with no timeouts.","test_case(): Conditionally GIC_EnableIRQ(87/88); Conditionally write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIOx_INTR); For i=0..31: write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + i*4, 0x00020000); wait_on(10); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1, 0x000000FF); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP2, 0x000000FF); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP3, 0x000000FF); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP4, 0x000000FF); wait_on(10); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, 0xFFFFFFFF); For i=0..31: write_reg(0xA0243FFC, 0x00000000); wait_on(10); int_pend=1; write_reg(0xA0243FFC, 0xFFFFFFFF); timeout=2000; while((int_pend==1) && (--timeout>0)) wait_on(10); if(timeout==0){ printf timeout; test_err++; break; } write_reg(0xA0243FFC, 0x00000000); wait_on(10); finish(test_err). Default_IRQHandler(): wr_val=1<<i; int_pend=0; rdata_grp=read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, 0x00000000); if((rdata_grp & 0xFFFFFFFF)==0){ printf error; test_err++; } For j=0..31: write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + j*4, 0x00010000); wait_on(2); rdata_grp=read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); if(rdata_grp!=0){ printf error; test_err++; } Conditionally write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIOx_INTR); read back and confirm cleared; write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, 0xFFFFFFFF); Conditionally GIC_ClearIRQ(87/88);","gp0_gpio_8; GP0_GPIO_9; GP0_GPIO_10; GP0_GPIO_11; GP0_GPIO_12; GP0_GPIO_13; GP0_GPIO_14; GP0_GPIO_15; GP0_GPIO_16; GP0_GPIO_17; GP0_GPIO_18; GP0_GPIO_19; GP0_GPIO_20; GP0_GPIO_21; GP0_GPIO_22; GP0_GPIO_23; GP0_GPIO_24; GP0_GPIO_25; GP0_GPIO_26; GP0_GPIO_27","MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8..MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27 (+ i*4); MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1; MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1; MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP2; MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP3; MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP4; MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1; LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO0_INTR; LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO1_INTR; MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1; LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR; LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO1_INTR","PASS if each pad 8–39 produces a positive-edge interrupt when enabled, the ISR confirms group status assertion, clears per-pin raw status, verifies group status clears, clears system-level status, and no timeouts occur.","Timeout loop must exit before timeout==0 (int_pend set to 0 by ISR). On ISR entry, group status read from MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1 must be nonzero; after writing 0x00010000 to each per-pin register, group status must read 0. After writing the appropriate LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIOx_INTR bit, a read indicates the bit is cleared. test_err remains 0 at finish().","NA","#include <lss_sysreg.h>; #include <stdio.h>; #include <test_define.c>; #include <test_common.h>","#define CNT 49","addr_array[20] = {MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8..MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27}; default_value_array[20] = {GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_DEFAULT_VAL..GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27_DEFAULT_VAL}; read_mask_array[20] = {GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_READ_MASK..GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27_READ_MASK}; write_mask_array[20] = {GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_WRITE_MASK..GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27_WRITE_MASK}; skip_array[20] = {0..0}"}]}